-- title:
--   Away-from-S Hecke points factor through newform eigencharacters
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$ be a natural number, let $S$ be a finite set of natural numbers containing every prime divisor of $N$, let $\mathcal{O}'$ be a commutative integral domain of characteristic zero, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ↑S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathcal{O}'$, where this Hecke algebra is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}} S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ generated by the operators `heckeTLin` attached to primes $\ell\nmid N$ with $\ell\notin S$ together with the operators `heckeULin` attached to primes $q\mid N$ with $q\notin S$. Then there exist a natural number $M_g\ge 1$ dividing $N$, a weight-two cusp form $g$ on $\Gamma_0(M_g)$ satisfying `g.IsNewform`, a ring homomorphism $\chi_g$ from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 ↑S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb{C}$ with $\chi_g(T_\ell)=a_\ell(g)$, the $\ell$-th coefficient of the $q$-expansion of $g$, for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid M_g$, and a ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the range of $\chi_g$ (a subring of $\mathbb{C}$) to $\mathcal{O}'$ such that for every prime $\ell\notin S$ with $\ell\nmid N$ one has $\iota(\chi_g(T_\ell))=\chi(T_\ell)$, the left-hand $T_\ell$ being the Hecke generator at level $M_g$ (legitimate since $M_g\mid N$) and the right-hand one that at level $N$. Here `IsNewform` for $g$ means: $g$ is a normalized eigenform, i.e. $a_1(g)=1$, $a_{mn}(g)=a_m(g)a_n(g)$ for coprime $m,n$, and the prime-power recursions $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)-p\,a_{p^{r}}(g)$ for primes $p\nmid M_g$ and $a_{p^{r+2}}(g)=a_p(g)a_{p^{r+1}}(g)$ for primes $p\mid M_g$; and moreover for no proper divisor $M$ of $M_g$ is there a normalized eigenform of level $M$ whose coefficients at all primes not dividing $M_g$ agree with those of $g$. No uniqueness of $M_g$, $g$, $\chi_g$ or $\iota$ is asserted, $\iota$ is not claimed injective, and nothing is asserted about the operators at primes dividing $N$ or lying in $S$.
--
--   This is the eigencharacter decomposition of the weight-two cuspidal Hecke algebra combined with Atkin–Lehner–Li newform theory, in the form used here: a characteristic-zero point of the anemic Hecke algebra away from $S$ is matched, prime by prime away from $N$ and $S$, with the Hecke eigensystem of a newform of level dividing $N$. It is the input to the constructions of Galois representations attached to Hecke eigensystems and to the local analysis of those representations at primes dividing the level.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_exists_isNewform_point_factor.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_Newforms

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.exists_isNewform_point_factor
    (N : ℕ) [NeZero N] (S : Finset ℕ)
    (_hNS : ∀ q : ℕ, q.Prime → q ∣ N → q ∈ S)
    (𝒪' : Type) [CommRing 𝒪'] [IsDomain 𝒪'] [CharZero 𝒪']
    (χ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 (↑S : Set ℕ) →+* 𝒪') :
    ∃ (Mg : ℕ) (_ : NeZero Mg) (_hMgN : Mg ∣ N)
      (g : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 Mg) 2) (_hg : g.IsNewform)
      (chig : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra Mg 2 (↑S : Set ℕ) →+* ℂ)
      (_hchig : ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓMg : ¬ ℓ ∣ Mg) (hℓS : ℓ ∉ (↑S : Set ℕ)),
        chig (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓMg hℓS) = ModularFormClass.qCoeff g ℓ)
      (iota : chig.range →+* 𝒪'),
      ∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓN : ¬ ℓ ∣ N) (hℓS : ℓ ∉ (↑S : Set ℕ)),
        iota (chig.rangeRestrict (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ
          (fun h => hℓN (h.trans _hMgN)) hℓS)) =
          χ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS) := by sorry
